Upstream and prior-work attribution
============================================================================

This firmware is a fork of, and builds on, the work of others. The detection
engine and several core mechanisms are derived from upstream code and research;
they retain their original names in the source as a provenance marker (see
docs/attribution.md for the full map). Credit is due to:

  * colonelpanichacks — "flock-you" firmware (https://github.com/colonelpanichacks/flock-you)
      The firmware this project was forked from. The promiscuous-mode WiFi
      detection engine, OUI matching, Flock information-element fingerprinting,
      SPIFFS session persistence, serial JSON emission, and LED/buzzer feedback
      derive from this project.

  * @NitekryDPaul — original research, initial firmware, and the Flock OUI
      target list that the detection method relies on.

  * Michael / @DeFlockJoplin (https://github.com/DeflockJoplin/flock-you) —
      research on the wildcard-probe-request signature of Flock infrastructure,
      and OUI contributions. (DeFlockJoplin forked the same upstream research
      base, not this repository.)

  * Pintor, Lucia & Atzori, Luigi (2022), "Analysis of Wi-Fi Probe Requests
      Towards Information Element Fingerprinting" — academic basis for the IE
      fingerprinting approach.

  * PlatformIO and PIOArduino for making MCU development easy and powerful

Original contributions in this repository (added after the fork) are Copyright
(c) 2026 Lone Crow Design, LLC and licensed under the MIT License.

